![logo](media/logo.png)

# ExcelDiff

A Windows desktop GUI diff tool for Excel / CSV / TSV. Can be used as a Git / Mercurial difftool.
Two products are built from the same source (EDR is the main build; EDN is retained as a fallback reference):

- **EDR** (main build, `ExcelDiffEDR.GUI.exe`): reads via ExcelDataReader. Fast reading (benchmark on a ~1.8 MB Excel file takes about 28% of EDN's time, ~72% faster); daily build / deploy / gate all target EDR.
- **EDN** (fallback build, `ExcelDiff.GUI.exe`): reads via NPOI. Most complete semantics; code is retained as the fallback for EDR blind spots and as a validation reference, but is not built / deployed in the daily flow.

The two builds are fully isolated (process / assembly / config / display name). UI language supports Chinese and English: the default is the language chosen in the setup wizard (recorded in the registry for the app to read), falling back to the system display language; a manual choice in Settings always wins.

![Demo](media/demo.gif)

![cell diff](media/cell_diff.png)

## Features

- Diff comparison: row-level + cell-level highlighting (`xls` / `xlsx` / `csv` / `tsv`).
- Resident + tray: single instance stays in the background; show / hide / exit.
- Single-instance IPC: a second invocation is routed to the resident instance over a named pipe, avoiding multiple windows.
- No-diff notification window: optional popup when the two files are identical (`NotifyEqual`).
- Window persistence: position / size / column width / row height / font / search history auto-saved.
- External localization: `lang\en-US.json` / `lang\zh-CN.json` (UTF-8).
- External command / file settings / color settings / diff log output.
- Start on boot (`StartOnBoot`).

## System Requirements

- Windows 7 SP1 or later
- .NET Framework 4.7.2

## Installing and uninstalling

### Install

Run the released `ExcelDiffSetup-<version>.exe` (administrator rights required). The wizard has 5 pages: **language** (defaults to the system display language; clicking a language re-languages the whole wizard immediately) → **location and components** → confirm → progress → finish.

- Default folder `%ProgramFiles%\ExcelDiffEDRTool`, changeable; the next install reuses the last location.
- Component defaults: desktop shortcut ✓ / start on boot ✓ / **Explorer context menu ✗** (tick it on that page if you want it).
- Silent install: `ExcelDiffSetup-<version>.exe /silent /dir="D:\Tools\ExcelDiffEDRTool" /components:shell,desktop,autostart /culture:en-US`.
  Switches: `/silent|/quiet`, `/uninstall`, `/install`, `/culture:zh-CN|en-US`, `/dir=<absolute path>` (relative paths and drive roots are refused), `/components:shell,desktop,autostart|none|all`, `/clearsettings`, `/log:<path>`, `/?`.
  Exit codes: `0` success / `1` failure / `2` help shown / `3` no payload / `4` invalid command line / `130` cancelled. **One exception**: an uninstall started from `Uninstall.exe` inside the install folder returns 0 to mean "handed over" (the copy it made in the temp folder does the work), so judge the result by whether the folder and the entry in "Apps & features" are gone.

After a successful install the install folder keeps a copy of the installer named **`Uninstall.exe`**.

### Uninstall

Any of these:

1. **Settings → Apps → ExcelDiffEDR → Uninstall** (or Control Panel → Programs and Features) — opens the uninstall wizard: language first, then a confirmation page, where you can also decide whether to delete the current user's settings.
2. **Double-click `Uninstall.exe` in the install folder** — same wizard; its default action is to uninstall, not to reinstall.
3. **Command line**: `Uninstall.exe /uninstall /silent` (silent; add `/clearsettings` to remove the user settings folder as well).

- **User settings are kept by default**: `%APPDATA%\ExcelDiffEDR.GUI\` is deleted only if you tick the box in the wizard or pass `/clearsettings`.
- Uninstall replays the `install-manifest.txt` written at install time: it removes only the files it placed there and empty folders, and **refuses outright when the manifest is missing** rather than guessing what a folder contains.
- If files are reported as in use (usually Explorer holding the shell extension), restart Explorer or sign out once, then run the uninstall again.
- To change components (e.g. add the context menu): download and run the installer again and tick the item (reinstall = uninstall then install, with rollback on failure). The component checkboxes are prefilled from **this run's** `/components:` switch, and fall back to the shipped defaults (desktop ✓ / start on boot ✓ / context menu ✗) when no switch was given; either way they are not prefilled from the current registration, so just tick what you want to add. The copy in the install folder uninstalls by default; pass `/install` explicitly to use it for a reinstall.

## Supported File Types

- `.xls`
- `.xlsx`
- `.csv`
- `.tsv`

## Build & Deploy

Uses `dotnet msbuild` (no standalone MSBuild); the reference-assembly root must be specified. `<repo>` below means the absolute path of the repository root (`git rev-parse --show-toplevel`).

### EDR (main build, ExcelDataReader) — output `ExcelDiffEDR.GUI.exe`

```
dotnet msbuild ExcelDiff.GUI/ExcelDiff.GUI.csproj /p:Configuration=Release /p:EdrRead=true /p:FrameworkPathOverride="<repo>\packages\refs\.NETFramework\v4.7.2" /p:IncludePackageReferencesDuringMarkupCompilation=false /p:GenerateResourceMSBuildArchitecture=CurrentArchitecture /p:GenerateResourceMSBuildRuntime=CurrentRuntime /t:Build /v:m /nologo
```

### EDN (fallback, NPOI read; code retained, not built daily) — output `ExcelDiff.GUI.exe`

Same as above without `/p:EdrRead=true` (default). Build manually only when an EDN fallback comparison is needed.

### Deploy order & resident restart

1. Build EDR → deploy EDR.
2. **Restart the EDR resident process right after every deploy** (kill process → relaunch with `--startup` from the deployed path).

Reason: the resident process starts from the deployed directory and locks the exe; without killing it the exe cannot be overwritten, and the old process keeps running in memory, distorting test results. The EDN (NPOI) fallback code is retained but not built / deployed in the daily flow.

### One-command verification gate

```
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File AI_Script\verify.ps1
```

All green = EDR main build compiles + installer project compiles + 31 NetDiff tests pass + `lang\*.json ↔ resx` in sync (both directions) + the two resx files carry the same key set + pitfall scans (no `Start-Process -Wait` on the forwarder, no hardcoded visible text in XAML).

The installer has its own release gate: `powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File AI_Script\verify-installer.ps1 -Install` (static checks on payload / embedded resources / version / bilingual key sets, plus A–M thirteen **real** install · uninstall · reinstall · rollback · refusal cases; needs admin, refuses to run when the machine already has an install record, and restores `HKCU Run` and the user settings folder afterwards).

## Usage

### From shortcut

![shortcut](media/shortcut.png)

### From command line

```
ExcelDiffEDR.GUI.exe [diff] <left file> <right file>
ExcelDiffEDR.GUI.exe [diff] -s <left file> -d <right file> [-c <tool>] [-i] [-w] [-v] [-e <name>]
```

- Left table = source file (`-s`), right table = destination file (`-d`). Positional files fill those two slots in the order written, at most two.
- The `diff` command word is optional. A first argument equal to `diff` / `none` / `merge` is treated as a command word (`merge` is not implemented and reports unknown command); anything else is treated as a file path.
- Do not mix positional files with explicit `-s` / `-d`. Invalid arguments (more than two positionals, mixing the two forms, an empty argument, a value option without a value) raise the `Invalid argument.` dialog.
- Quote paths that contain spaces.

| Option | Description | Type | Default |
|--------|-------------|------|---------|
| `-s` `--src-path` | Source file path. | string | |
| `-d` `--dst-path` | Dest file path. | string | |
| `-c` `--external-cmd` | Activate an external tool for unsupported file types or on exception. | string | |
| `-i` `--immediately-execute-external-cmd` | Execute external cmd without an error dialog. | bool | false |
| `-w` `--wait-external-cmd` | Wait for the external process to finish. | bool | false |
| `-v` `--validate-extension` | Validate extension before opening a file. | bool | false |
| `-e` `--empty-file-name` | Empty file name. | string | |

> Single-instance IPC: if a resident instance is already running, a new command-line invocation is forwarded to it over a named pipe and the caller exits immediately. A resident launched with `--startup` runs hidden in the tray.

### Git difftool

`.gitconfig` (`<install dir>` = where the app is actually installed: the setup wizard defaults to `%ProgramFiles%\ExcelDiffEDRTool`, changeable in the wizard or by adding `/dir=<absolute path>` to **the setup package you downloaded** (`ExcelDiffSetup-<version>.exe`) - the `Uninstall.exe` inside the install folder only uninstalls; the EDR main build ships `ExcelDiffEDR.GUI.exe`, the EDN build ships `ExcelDiff.GUI.exe`)

```
[diff]
tool = ExcelDiff

[difftool "ExcelDiff"]
cmd = \"<install dir>/ExcelDiffEDR.GUI.exe\" diff -s \"$LOCAL\" -d \"$REMOTE\" -c WinMerge -i -w -v

[alias]
windiff = difftool -g -y -t ExcelDiff
```

### Fork external diff tool

Fork → Settings → External Diff Tools → Add:

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| Name | `EDR` (any name) |
| Path | `<install dir>\ExcelDiffEDR.GUI.exe` |
| Arguments | `"$REMOTE" "$LOCAL"` |

- **The first placeholder fills the left table, the second the right table** (positional files fill `-s` / `-d` in order), so "remote on the left, local on the right" is `"$REMOTE" "$LOCAL"`; written explicitly that is `diff -s "$REMOTE" -d "$LOCAL"`. The sides follow the values after `-s` / `-d`, not the order in which the two flags are written.
- `$LOCAL` / `$REMOTE` are the two temporary file placeholders Fork passes in. **Keep the quotes** (the temp directory may contain spaces). After configuring, run one comparison and read the "Source / Destination" path boxes at the top of the window to confirm the sides.
- Optional flags: `-v` validates the extension before opening, `-c <tool> -i` hands unsupported types straight to an external tool without an error dialog.
- **Resident process and "waiting for external tool"**: ExcelDiff is designed to stay resident in the tray, so the process does not exit when a window closes. If no resident instance is running, the process Fork starts becomes the resident one and **never exits**, so Fork keeps waiting. Start the resident instance first (`ExcelDiffEDR.GUI.exe --startup`); after that every call is forwarded to it and exits immediately. The resident's integrity level must match the interactive desktop's — on a mismatch a Fork started from the desktop cannot reach it over the named pipe (UIPI). "Match" is not the same as "must be non-elevated": on a machine with UAC disabled, explorer, Fork and the app all run High.

### Mercurial difftool

`mercurial.ini`

```
[merge-tools]
exceldiff.executable = <install dir>\ExcelDiffEDR.GUI.exe
exceldiff.diffargs = diff -s $parent1 -d $child -c WinMerge -i -w -v -e empty

[tortoisehg]
vdiff = exceldiff
```

> Adjust paths to your actual deployment directory; benchmark comparisons use EDR, EDN serves as the fallback validation reference.

### Explorer context menu

`ExcelDiff.ShellExtension` is a COM shell extension and is **not ticked by default on page 2 of the setup wizard**. To get "ExcelDiffEDR" when you right-click a single file in Explorer, tick "Add the Explorer context menu" there (no Explorer restart is needed - setup notifies the shell; if registration fails during an uninstall/reinstall, restart Explorer once). To add it later, download and run the installer again with that box ticked (the component checkboxes are prefilled from this run's `/components:` switch, otherwise from the shipped defaults - desktop ✓ / start on boot ✓ / context menu ✗ - and never from the current registration, so tick only what you want to add).

![context menu](media/context.png)

## Register External Command

Specify an external command via the `--external-cmd` command-line argument.

![external command window](media/ext_cmd_win.png)

### Available Variables

| Value | Description |
|-------|-------------|
| `${SRC}` | Source file path |
| `${DST}` | Dest file path |

It can also be executed from within the tool.

![external command](media/ext_cmd.png)

## File Settings / Color Settings

- File settings: specify a row header or a column header for each file.
- Color settings: customize background colors (alternating rows / column header / row header / added / removed / modified / modified row).

![file settings](media/file_settings.png)

![color settings](media/settings.png)

## Shortcut Keys

| Shortcut Key | Description |
|--------------|-------------|
| Ctrl + → | Next modified cell |
| Ctrl + ← | Previous modified cell |
| Ctrl + ↓ | Next modified row |
| Ctrl + ↑ | Previous modified row |
| Ctrl + K | Next added row |
| Ctrl + I | Previous added row |
| Ctrl + L | Next removed row |
| Ctrl + O | Previous removed row |
| Ctrl + F | Search cell |
| F9 | Next match cell |
| F8 | Previous match cell |
| Ctrl + C | Copy selected cells as TSV |
| Ctrl + Shift + C | Copy selected cells as CSV |
| Ctrl + D | Show(Hide) console |
| Ctrl + B | Output selected cells diff as log |

## Output Diff as Log

Press `Ctrl + D` or choose "Output log" from the context menu to output the diff as a log.
The format can be changed in the "diff extraction settings".

![log](media/log.png)

## No-Diff Window & Language Switch

- **No-diff window**: shown when the two files are identical and `NotifyEqual` is enabled. Close it with the top-right "X" or ESC (closes only the dialog); the red "Exit" button (triggered by Enter) also closes the comparison window.
- **Language switch**: after switching the language in settings, the app closes to apply the change; the next diff command recreates the window with the new language.

## Settings & Persistence

Settings are saved as YAML at:

```
%APPDATA%\<assembly name>\<assembly name>.yml
```

- EDR: `%APPDATA%\ExcelDiffEDR.GUI\`
- EDN: `%APPDATA%\ExcelDiff.GUI\`

## Regression Verification

- `AI_Script\verify.ps1`: one-command gate (EDR main build + installer project compile + 31 NetDiff tests + `lang ↔ resx` sync both directions + matching resx key sets + pitfall scans).
- `AI_Script\verify-installer.ps1`: installer release gate (static checks; `-Install` adds A–M thirteen real install/uninstall/reinstall/rollback/refusal cases, needs admin).
- `DiffHarness\`: headless diff comparison (deterministic diff text of EDN/EDR outputs).
- `NetDiff\NetDiff.TestRunner\`: offline algorithm unit-test runner.

## Known Problems

- If there are column deletions or additions, they may not be displayed at the expected position. Specify an appropriate header and re-extract the diff:
  1. Select the appropriate header cell.
  2. Right-click to show the context menu.
  3. Choose "Extract diff with this row as header".

